sec.p:
PepGraphormer constructs a heterogeneous graph comprising sequence nodes (representing peptides) and amino acid nodes (representing single residues). The graph's edges are strategically weighted by two principles to capture both local and global information. First, sequence-to-amino-acid edges are weighted using TF-IDF [38] to define the distinctive amino acid composition of each local peptide. Second, amino-acid-to-amino-acid edges are weighted based on PMI [39] to model the global statistical co-occurrence between residue pairs across the entire dataset. This dual-edge strategy is designed to reveal key amino acid motifs and underlying functional associations, providing a rich semantic foundation for pattern propagation from labeled to unlabeled sequences. The adjacency matrix A of this graph is formulated as shown in Eq. (1).1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
