				\begin{document}$${{\boldsymbol{X}}}_{seq}^{i}$$\end{document}Xseqi, by applying an average pooling operation across the final-layer representation vectors of all valid amino acid residues from the ESM2 output. This sequence-level embedding captures a global semantic fingerprint of the peptide, encapsulating not only amino acid composition but also crucial information regarding sequence order, long-range dependencies, and latent evolutionary features learned during pre-training.3\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
